# SAMSUNG — DAX Measures

This document describes the DAX measures used in the SAMSUNG Power BI model. It is written in a documentation style so you can copy/paste each measure into your model or use it as a reference.

If you exported the model via DAX Studio or have an "All Measures" table, the original DAX is preserved under each measure's DAX section.

---

## How this document is organized

For each measure you'll find:
- Name: The measure name as it appears in the model (heading).
- DAX: The measure formula in a DAX code block.
- Format: Suggested display formatting for visuals.
- Description: Short explanation of what the measure returns and where it is used.
- Dependencies / Notes: Any supporting measures, columns, or assumptions.

---

## Measures

### Avg Load Time
Name: Avg_Load_Time

```dax
Avg_Load_Time = AVERAGE(fact_procurement[lead_time_days])
```
Format: Decimal number

Description: Calculates the average procurement lead time (in days) using the lead_time_days column from the fact_procurement table.

Dependencies / Notes:
- Requires fact_procurement[lead_time_days] to be numeric.

---

### Days of Inventory
Name: Days_of_Inventory

```dax
Days_of_Inventory = DIVIDE(365, [Turnover_Rate])
```
Format: Whole number

Description: Estimates how many days the current inventory level can support based on the inventory turnover rate.

Dependencies / Notes:
- Depends on the [Turnover_Rate] measure (documented below).
- Handle zero/blank turnover_rate to avoid divide-by-zero errors.

---

### Defect Rate
Name: Defect_Rate

```dax
Defect_Rate = SUM(fact_production[defective_units])
```
Format: Whole number

Description: Calculates the total number of defective production units from the fact_production table.

Dependencies / Notes:
- If a percentage is required, divide by total units produced.

---

### Delivered %
Name: Delivered %

```dax
Delivered % = DIVIDE([total_delivered_ship],[Total_Shipment])
```
Format: Percentage

Description: Measures the percentage of shipments that were successfully delivered.

Dependencies / Notes:
- Relies on [total_delivered_ship] and [Total_Shipment] measures being defined and returning numeric values.

---

### Discount
Name: discount

```dax
discount = SUM(fact_sales[discount_amount])
```
Format: Currency

Description: Calculates the total discount amount applied to sales.

Dependencies / Notes:
- Uses fact_sales[discount_amount]. Ensure currency formatting is applied where needed.

---

### Discount %
Name: Discount %

```dax
Discount % =
VAR product_amt = [discount]+[Total_Revenue]
RETURN
DIVIDE([discount],product_amt)
```
Format: Percentage

Description: Calculates discounts as a percentage of gross amount (discount + revenue).

Dependencies / Notes:
- Depends on [discount] and [Total_Revenue]. Use DIVIDE to protect against division-by-zero.

---

### Growth Revenue
Name: Growth_Revenue

```dax
Growth_Revenue =
VAR curr_rev = [Total_Revenue]
VAR prev_rev =
    CALCULATE(
        [Total_Revenue],
        SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(dim_date[date])
    )
RETURN
DIVIDE(curr_rev-prev_rev,prev_rev)
```
Format: Percentage

Description: Calculates year-over-year revenue growth using SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR over the date dimension.

Dependencies / Notes:
- Requires a properly configured date table (dim_date) marked as a date table.

